{title: More About Jesus}
{artist: Eliza E. Hewitt / John R. Sweney}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: G}
{key_original: Ab}
{tempo: 65}
{time: 6/8}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Pentecostal Hymns Nos. 1 and 2 Combined (Chicago, Illinois: Hope Publishing, 1894), # 1)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]More about Jesus would I know,
[D]More of His grace to [G]others show;
[G]More of His saving fullness see,
[G]More of His love who died for me.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[G]More, more about Jesus,
[D]More, more about [G]Jesus;
[G]More of His saving fullness see,
[G]More of His love who died for me.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]More about Jesus let me learn,
[D]More of His holy [G]will discern;
[G]Spirit of God, my teacher be,
[G]Showing the things of Christ to me.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]More about Jesus; in His Word,
[D]Holding communion [G]with my Lord;
[G]Hearing His voice in every line,
[G]Making each faithful saying mine.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]More about Jesus; on His throne,
[D]Riches in glory [G]all His own;
[G]More of His kingdom’s sure increase;
[G]More of His coming, Prince of Peace.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
